=== width 80, default
\e[1m\e[3m\e[4:2mChangelog\e[24m\e[23m\e[22m

All notable changes are documented here.

\e[1m\e[4m[Unreleased]\e[24m\e[22m

\e[1mAdded\e[22m

• A \e[38;5;3m--dry-run\e[39m flag that shows what would change without touching a file.
• Support for \e[38;5;3m~/.config/frobnicate/frobnicate.toml\e[39m, read before the project's
  own file.

\e[1mFixed\e[22m

• A crash when a file name contained a combining character, such as \e[38;5;3mé\e[39m.
• The progress bar overwrote the last line of the output on narrow terminals; it
  now stays within the terminal width.

\e[1m\e[4m[2.1.0] - 2026-09-12\e[24m\e[22m

\e[1mChanged\e[22m

• Jobs default to the number of CPU cores, up to \e[38;5;3m8\e[39m.
• Error messages name the file first, then the reason.

\e[1mDeprecated\e[22m

• \e[38;5;3m--legacy-output\e[39m, which will go away in 3.0. Use \e[38;5;3m--format=plain\e[39m.

\e[1m\e[4m[2.0.0] - 2026-05-02\e[24m\e[22m

\e[1mRemoved\e[22m

• The \e[38;5;3m--old-syntax\e[39m flag and the \e[38;5;3m.frobrc\e[39m file.

\e[1mChanged\e[22m

• \e[1mBreaking:\e[22m the exit code for partial failure is \e[38;5;3m1\e[39m, no longer \e[38;5;3m3\e[39m.
